# The level 52 Rogue class chain: A Simple Request (8233) from your class
# leaders to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, then Sealed Azure Bag (8234) and Encoded
# Fragments (8235) with Archmage Xylem in Azshara, and The Azure Key (8236)
# from Morphaz in the Sunken Temple back to Lord Ravenholdt.
# Forever change? Forever's Rogue class quest list (data/local/quest-audit/)
# says The Azure Key no longer offers its reward choices (Duskbat Drape, Ebon
# Mask, Whisperwalk Boots), but the same list's row and Forever's quest data
# (quest 8236, checked 2026-10-29) still list three choices (19982, 19984,
# 20255), so the guide names no item and says to look.
# INGAME: does The Azure Key (8236) still offer the Duskbat Drape, Ebon Mask or Whisperwalk Boots on Forever, or only experience, money and reputation?
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json and items.json for the givers, drops and
# spawns; travel.json for the flight points; the quest text of The Azure Key
# (quest 8236) for Morphaz's lair. Morphaz has no spawn in
# the data: he is an elite boss inside the Sunken Temple, a dungeon; the
# entrance point is the one alliance/40-50/07-un-goro-crater uses for the
# temple (Swamp of Sorrows 69.9,53.6), which matches the point from players' reports
# used by
# class/hunter/the-hunters-charm.
# Based on data, not play: the beta caps at level 30 until launch on
# 4 November, so nothing here has been checked in game.
# The KB drops table: Sealed Azure Bag 3.7% from Timbermaw Shamans (50),
# Encoded Fragment 80% from Forest Oozes (52). data/local/mechanics
# (quest-steps and quest-notes, checked 2026-10-20): pickpocketing the bag
# without Timbermaw reputation loss and the At War toggle, the level 47-49
# furbolgs without it, the ooze groups and pickpocketing them, Morphaz linked
# with Hazzas and his 24 hour respawn, killing at the manor turning Lord
# Jorach away. Morphaz's spawn order (the six balcony trolls open Jammal'an;
# his death brings Weaver and Dreamscythe; theirs brings Morphaz and Hazzas):
# public Classic dungeon guides (2024); Forever's data has no spawns inside.
# ASSUMED: Morphaz and Hazzas appear only after Weaver and Dreamscythe die, and those two only after Jammal'an (Classic flow; Forever's data has no spawns or events inside the Sunken Temple). In-game check: the drakes' order in the Pit of Sacrifice.

step A Simple Request (Alliance)
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip At 50 Osborne the Night Man in Stormwind's Old Town has it; so do Syurna in Darnassus and Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.
  level 50
  accept 8233 npc 918                         -- Osborne the Night Man

step A Simple Request (Horde)
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip At 50 Ormok in the Cleft of Shadow has it; so does Miles Dexter in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter.
  level 50
  accept 8233 npc 3328                        -- Ormok

step Lord Jorach Ravenholdt
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Ravenholdt Manor hides in the hills east of Tarren Mill. Horde fly to Tarren Mill, Alliance to Southshore. The trail starts behind the plateau north of Durnholde Keep, climbs into the hills and runs through a small tunnel into the Alterac Mountains; Lord Jorach is inside the manor. Do not attack anyone at the manor: lost Ravenholdt reputation makes him refuse to speak to you.
  turnin 8233                                 -- Lord Jorach Ravenholdt
  accept 8234

step Sealed Azure Bag
  zone Azshara
  tip Alliance fly to Talrendis Point, Horde to Valormok. Only the level 50-51 Timbermaw Shamans in the furbolg hills of northern Azshara carry the bag (the level 47-49 furbolgs further south do not): about one kill in thirty drops it. Pick Pocket them instead and you lose no Timbermaw reputation; if you are Unfriendly or better with Timbermaw Hold, mark them At War in your reputation panel first. They cast Lightning Bolt and Lightning Cloud, heal each other and run at low health.
  getfp "Talrendis Point" only Alliance
  getfp "Valormok" only Horde
  collect 19775 quest 8234.1                  -- Sealed Azure Bag: Timbermaw Shaman

step Archmage Xylem
  tip Sanath Lim-yo, camped below the cliffs just east of Valormok, teleports you up (dismount first); a trail leads to Xylem's tower.
  turnin 8234                                 -- Archmage Xylem
  accept 8235

step Encoded Fragments
  tip The Forest Oozes (level 52-53, Diseased Slime up close) drop a fragment four times in five: the biggest group, seven of them, is in the Bitter Reaches hills of north-eastern Azshara, four more south-east of Valormok. Pick their pockets before the kill for an extra fragment or two. Killing the Mistwing Ravagers and hippogryphs that share their spots makes more oozes appear.
  collect 20023 x10 quest 8235.1              -- Encoded Fragment: Forest Ooze

step Back to Xylem
  turnin 8235                                 -- Archmage Xylem
  accept 8236

step Morphaz in the Sunken Temple
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip Morphaz, a level 52 elite green drake, lives deep in the Sunken Temple: a group of five, level 50-54. The temple stands in the Pool of Tears; climb into the sunken building, swim down through it and follow the passage to the portal. Horde: fly to Stonard; Alliance: fly to Nethergarde Keep and ride on. He is not there when you arrive: first kill the six troll guardians (elites of 50-52) on the platforms around the upper ring, which opens the way down (the left-hand ramp from the entrance) to Jammal'an the Prophet in the Pit of Sacrifice. Jammal'an's death brings out two drakes, Weaver and Dreamscythe; when both are dead, Morphaz and Hazzas appear together and fight as a pair. Their Acid Breath is nature damage: nature protection potions help; poisons and Blind do not work on them. The key always drops. Hunters, Priests and Mages of 50 need Morphaz too: one clear serves them all.
  collect 20022 quest 8236.1 @69.9,53.6       -- Azure Key: Morphaz, inside the temple

step Lord Ravenholdt
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Look at the reward window before you hand in: Classic offered the Duskbat Drape, the Ebon Mask or the Whisperwalk Boots, and Forever's notes say the choice may be gone.
  turnin 8236                                 -- Lord Jorach Ravenholdt
